<title>MEXICO: Mexlub seeks listing on Mexican bourse.</title>
<headline>Mexlub seeks listing on Mexican bourse.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexicana de Lubricantes (Mexlub) has filed a preliminary application to trade on the Mexico Stock Exchange,  company Chairman Salvador Martinez Garza said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Mexlub was created in 1993 in a joint venture of state oil monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos and Impulsora Jalisciense. Pemex owns 49 percent of the company.</p>
<p>Mexlub produces motor oils and lubricants in five plants in Sinaloa, Nuevo Leon, Puebla, Jalisco and the state of Mexico.</p>
<p>In an interview with Reuters, Martinez Garza said Mexlub would end 1996 with a net profit of 120 million pesos, compared with a 110 million peso profit in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara bureau +523 817-0397</p>
